# 5. SLOW-MOVING FUNDAMENTALS

Do not imply that slow-moving economic or resource indicators update every day.

Only discuss these when new official data have appeared or the situation has materially changed:

* U.S. Strategic Petroleum Reserve
* U.S. commercial crude stocks
* gasoline inventories
* distillate inventories
* global petroleum inventories
* U.S. crude production
* physical Hormuz oil flows
* CPI inflation
* PCE inflation
* payrolls
* unemployment
* GDP
* private domestic demand
* Federal Reserve policy
* Treasury borrowing
* fiscal deficit
* defense-production rates
* confirmed weapons-production contracts

When new EIA weekly petroleum data are available, explicitly compare:

* SPR level,
* commercial crude,
* gasoline,
* distillates,
* change from the preceding week,
* five-year seasonal norms when available.

The Strategic Petroleum Reserve is an emergency government stockpile, not the total supply of petroleum available to the United States.

Never convert SPR depletion into statements such as:

**"The United States has only X days of oil remaining."**

unless an authoritative source is specifically making a different and properly defined calculation.

